# This repo: `wwn-vms`

Machines kind **`virtual_machine`**. Not containers, not Wasm packages, not
Desktop/LockScreen, not Swinging Bridge.

## Mode A vs Mode B (design both)

| | Mode A (store) | Mode B |
|---|---|---|
| iOS / iPadOS | UTM-SE-class **jitless** QEMU-TCTI | UTM/QEMU **+ JIT** (TrollStore and/or Sileo Mode B IPA) |
| tvOS / watchOS / visionOS | **Forbidden** | **Forbidden** |
| macOS | **QEMU + HVF** (Hypervisor.framework) | Same (macOS is not App Store constrained) |
| Android | QEMU + KVM when present, else TCG+JIT | Root/privileged outside Play |

- **Never** link JIT Mode B into App Store / Play artifacts.
- tvOS / watchOS / visionOS: VM kinds **forbidden** (policy).
- iOS: TrollStore = JIT + Desktop/LockScreen, without Swinging Bridge. Sileo adds the full jailbreak surface. See Wawona `wawona-ios-mode-b-channels`.
- Per-OS backends differ. Do not force one QEMU binary onto every host.
- Leave active Apple Container work in `wwn-containers` alone unless asked.

Accel lane: `capabilities.nix` (`hvf` / `tcti` / `android-hv`).
Rust argv helper: `crates/wwn-vms-engine` (`Tcti` vs `TcgJit`).

Canonical: `Wawona/docs/vms-mode-a-b.md`, `mode-a-b.md`, `wawona-product-map`.
